        thingsToDo: `Vero Beach's Atlantic beaches rank among Florida's best, with less crowding than more famous destinations. The McKee Botanical Garden offers 18 acres of tropical plants and water features, providing peaceful recovery time between games. For wildlife encounters, the Environmental Learning Center offers kayak tours through Indian River Lagoon mangroves. The Navy SEAL Museum tells fascinating stories of naval special operations and includes hands-on exhibits kids love. Historic downtown Vero Beach features antique shops, galleries, and the Theatre Plaza for catching movies. The Vero Beach Museum of Art provides rainy day cultural enrichment. For active recovery, the Jungle Trail offers 8 miles of scenic driving and biking through hammock terrain. Sebastian Inlet State Park, 15 minutes south, delivers excellent fishing, surfing, and wildlife viewing. The relaxed pace here offers genuine recovery for travel ball families accustomed to frenetic tournament weekends.`,
